{
  "abstract": "Lean 4 proof of the Erdős–Rado theorem that every red/blue colouring of the 3-element subsets of the reals, ordered as usual, has either a red set of order type ω + n or a blue set of four reals, for every finite n ≥ 2 (the partition relation 𝔠 → (ω + n, 4)³ of Erdős and Rado, 1956, Theorem 31). It is a positive partial answer to Erdős Problem 70. The development includes infinite Ramsey theorems for pairs and triples on ℕ and lemmas on uncountable sets of reals.",
